# STIG CNTR-K8-000160: The Kubernetes Scheduler must use TLS 1.2, at a minimum, to 
# STIG ID: V-242377 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `k8s-cntr-k8-000160-sched-tls-min-version-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `kubernetes`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CNTR-K8-000160: The Kubernetes Scheduler must use TLS 1.2, at a minimum, to protect the confiden`
    description `The Kubernetes Scheduler must use TLS 1.2, at a minimum, to protect the confidentiality of sensitive data during electronic dissemination.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `kubernetes,stig,disa-stig,kube-scheduler`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CNTR-K8-000160,NIST-800-53:AC-17(2)`
    control_objective `AC-17(2)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Kubernetes:cluster:k8s-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for CNTR-K8-000160.`

    component_id `comp-k8s-cluster`

    impl_AC_17_2 `This control is validated by checking the required Kubernetes configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT kube_scheduler_pod
        kind `Pod`
        namespace `kube-system`
        label_selector `component=kube-scheduler`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE flag_check
        found boolean = true
        record
            field spec.containers.0.command string contains `--tls-min-version` at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN k8s_resource
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF flag_check
            OBJECT_REF kube_scheduler_pod
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
